cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IntentLab in teaching or research, cite this software and the original data and methods listed in NOTICE.md."
type: software
title: "IntentLab: recorded motor-imagery EEG decoding and selective prediction"
authors:
  - name: "Jayashruthi Rajesh Babu"
    website: "https://jayashruthi.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shrut10/intentlab-bci"
url: "https://intentlab-bci.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  An open-source teaching and research demonstration of motor-imagery EEG
  decoding, participant-disjoint evaluation, confidence-based abstention and
  channel sensitivity, with a separate exploratory study of personal calibration
  and Euclidean alignment. The recorded-data experiments do not establish
  reliable live control. Cite the specific commit used for reproducibility.
keywords:
  - EEG
  - motor imagery
  - brain-computer interface
  - selective prediction
  - reproducible research
